-- title:
--   Frobenius descent for π-nilpotent algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, with $\pi$ irreducible, residue ring $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ of cardinality $r$, and $(r) = (\pi)$ (so $\mathcal{O}$ is absolutely unramified with residue field $\mathbb{F}_r$). Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, such that every $x \in Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $(\pi)$ and every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $(\pi)$, and let $\mathrm{Fr}$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism of $Onr$ with $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{(\pi)}$ for all $x$. Fix $m > 0$ and write $S$ for the equalizer of $\mathrm{Fr}^{m}$ and the identity, i.e. the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{Fr}^{m}$-fixed elements of $Onr$; let $\mathrm{FrS}$ be an $S$-algebra automorphism of $Onr$ acting as $\mathrm{Fr}^{m}$ on every element. Let $B$ be a commutative ring which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra and an $S$-algebra compatibly, in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent. Then every $z \in B \otimes_{S} Onr$ fixed by $\mathrm{id}_B \otimes \mathrm{FrS}$ is of the form $b \otimes 1$ for a unique $b \in B$.
--
--   This is the affine case of descent of scalars along the Frobenius for the unramified extension $S \subset Onr$: the fixed ring of $1 \otimes \mathrm{Fr}^{m}$ on $B \otimes_{S} Onr$ is exactly $B$, for $B$ a $\pi$-nilpotent algebra. It rests on the description of the $\mathrm{Fr}^{m}$-fixed levels of $Onr$ given by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.fixedPoints_frobenius_levels`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.fixedPoints_frobenius_levels), and is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the project to descend morphisms to, and opens of, the spectra occurring in the formal upper half plane functor along the Frobenius twist.
